# Notebook outputs are kept in the repository for the whole drafting phase.
#
# Every notebook here is under review by two TAs who are asked to run it end to
# end and flag unexpected outputs, so the outputs have to be readable on GitHub
# without running anything. Stripping happens once, at the end, in the script
# that generates the student-facing repository.
#
# This also removes a trap: with the filter on, any notebook uploaded through
# the GitHub web interface keeps its outputs in the commit but shows up as
# locally modified on every clone, because the filter strips it again at diff
# time. Eight notebooks were in that state before this change.
#
# To turn stripping back on, uncomment the two lines below and run once:
#   nbstripout --install --attributes .gitattributes
#
# *.ipynb filter=nbstripout
# *.zpln filter=nbstripout
